      "section": "Kidney nuclei",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "A mouse kidney section imaged in three fluorescence channels, projected along z and stored as a three-level pyramid. Each point is a nucleus segmented on the 450 nm channel. Toggle channels and adjust their contrast in the viewer, then draw a lasso around some nuclei: the table and the cards follow the selection.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
