      "title_size": "sm",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "About these examples",
      "order": 4,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Each tab shows one kind of image: several fluorescence channels, a stained section with spatial spots, a 3D stack over time and one store per sample (all OME-Zarr), then a pyramidal OME-TIFF and a SpatialData store. The images are scikit-image sample datasets (CC0, public domain or without known restrictions). Cells and spots are computed from the pixels; time courses, counts and conditions are synthetic. Nothing here is a result.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    }
